Input: {"question": "What is the modern-day name of Abdera?", "original_source_segments": {"D1S1": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0220-2de71d129fab:d00", "start": 0, "end": 145, "text": "Abdera, Spain Abdera was an ancient Carthaginian and Roman port on a hill above the modern Adra on the southeastern Mediterranean coast of Spain."}, "D1S2": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0220-2de71d129fab:d00", "start": 146, "end": 264, "text": "It was located between Malaca (now Málaga) and Carthago Nova (now Cartagena) in the district inhabited by the Bastuli."}, "D1S3": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0220-2de71d129fab:d00", "start": 265, "end": 338, "text": "Abdera shares its name with a city in Thrace and another in North Africa."}, "D1S4": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0220-2de71d129fab:d00", "start": 339, "end": 373, "text": "Its coins bore the inscription ()."}, "D1S5": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0220-2de71d129fab:d00", "start": 374, "end": 573, "text": "The first element in the name appears to be the Punic word for \"servant\" or \"slave\"; the second element seems shared by the Phoenician names for Agadir (now Cadiz) and Cythera but of unclear meaning."}, "D1S6": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0220-2de71d129fab:d00", "start": 574, "end": 584, "text": "It appears"}, "D2S1": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0220-2de71d129fab:d01", "start": 0, "end": 570, "text": "Adra , Spain - Wikipedia Jump to content Main menu Main menu move to sidebar hide Navigation Main page Contents Current events Random article About Wikipedia Contact us Contribute Help Learn to edit Community portal Recent changes Upload file Special pages Search Search Appearance Donate Create account Log in Personal tools Donate Create account Log in Pages for logged out editors learn more Contributions Talk Contents move to sidebar hide ( Top ) 1 History 2 Demographics 3 Culture in Adra 4 People Toggle People subsection 4.1 C 4.2 F 4.