North Africa."}, "D5S2": {"document_number": 5, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0220-2de71d129fab:d04", "start": 35, "end": 145, "text": "It was variously hellenized as \"Ábdēra\" (), \"Ábdēron\" (), and \"Ábdēros\" () before being latinized as \"Abdera\"."}, "D5S3": {"document_number": 5, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0220-2de71d129fab:d04", "start": 146, "end": 386, "text": "(Unusually, it was declined as a 2nd-declension masculine noun despite having a terminal \"a\".) Greek legend attributed the name to an eponymous \"Abderus\" who fell nearby and was memorialized by Hercules's founding of a city at the location."}, "D5S4": {"document_number": 5, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0220-2de71d129fab:d04", "start": 387, "end": 460, "text": "The present-day town is written Avdira () and pronounced in modern Greek."}, "D5S5": {"document_number": 5, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0220-2de71d129fab:d04", "start": 461, "end": 625, "text": "The Phoenicians apparently began the settlement of Abdera at some point before the mid-7th century and the town long maintained Phoenician standards in its coinage."}, "D5S6": {"document_number": 5, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0220-2de71d129fab:d04", "start": 626, "end": 635, "text": "The Greek"}}, "original_cards": [{"doc_id": "ramdocs-0220-2de71d129fab:d00", "card_id": "ramdocs-0220-2de71d129fab:d00:c0", "entity": "Abdera", "scope": "modern-day name", "claim": "Abdera was an ancient Carthaginian and Roman port on a hill above the modern Adra on the southeastern Mediterranean coast of Spain.", "answer": "Adra", "quote": "Abdera, Spain Abdera was an ancient Carthaginian and Roman port on a hill above the modern Adra on the southeastern Mediterranean coast of Spain.", "original_document_number": 1}, {"doc_id": "ramdocs-0220-2de71d129fab:d01", "card_id": "ramdocs-0220-2de71d129fab:d01:c0", "entity": "Abdera", "scope": "modern-day name", "claim": "The modern-day name of Abdera is Adra, Spain.", "answer": "Adra", "quote": "Adra , Spain - Wikipedia Jump to content Main menu Main menu move to sidebar hide Navigation Main page Contents Current events Random article About Wikipedia Contact us Contribute Help Learn to edit Community portal Recent changes Upload file Special pages Search Search Appearance Donate Create account Log in Personal tools Donate Create account Log in Pages for logged out editors learn more Contributions Talk Contents move to sidebar hide ( Top ) 1 History 2 Demographics 3 Culture in Adra 4 People Toggle People subsection 4.1 C 4.2 F 4.3 G 4.4 L 4.5 O 4.6 R 4.7 S", "original_document_number": 2}, {"doc_id": "ramdocs-0220-2de71d129fab:d04", "card_id": "ramdocs-0220-2de71d129fab:d04:c0", "entity": "Abdera", "scope": "modern-day name", "claim": "The present-day town is written Avdira.", "answer": "Avdira", "quote": "The present-day town is written Avdira () and pronounced in modern Greek.", "original_document_number": 5}], "current_answers": ["Adra", "Avdira"], "candidate_answers": [{"candidate_id": "R0", "answer": "Adra", "origin": "initial"}, {"candidate_id": "R1", "answer": "Avdira", "origin": "initial"}]}

